{"name":"Monsoon Season","hex":"#839ab0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"monsoon season","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of the year when the monsoon occurs, the rainy season."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monsoon_season"}],"entries":[{"title":"Monsoon Season","blocks":[{"text":"Monsoon Season is the debut mixtape from Hanumankind. The mixtape was released on July 25, 2025, via Capitol Records, Def Jam Recordings, and Universal Music Group. The project features collaborations with artists such as A$AP Rocky, Denzel Curry, Maxo Kream, Roisee, and Rudy Mukta."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d5/Monsoon.Season.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monsoon_Season","wikidata":"Q137803390"},{"title":"Wet season","blocks":[{"text":"The wet season is the time of year when most of a region's average annual rainfall occurs. Generally, the season lasts at least one month. The term green season is also sometimes used as a euphemism by tourist authorities. Areas with wet seasons are dispersed across portions of the tropics and subtropics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Cairns_climate.svg/330px-Cairns_climate.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wet_season","wikidata":"Q3117517"},{"title":"Monsoon","blocks":[{"text":"A monsoon is traditionally a seasonal reversing wind accompanied by corresponding changes in precipitation, but now used to describe seasonal changes in atmospheric circulation and precipitation associated with annual latitudinal oscillation of the Intertropical Convergence Zone, specifically between its limits to the north and south of the equator."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Monsoon_clouds_near_Nagercoil.jpg/330px-Monsoon_clouds_near_Nagercoil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monsoon","wikidata":"Q42967"},{"title":"Season","blocks":[{"text":"A season is a division of the year based on changes in weather, ecology, and the number of daylight hours in a given region. On Earth, seasons are the result of the axial parallelism of Earth's tilted orbit around the Sun. In temperate and polar regions, the seasons are marked by changes in the intensity of sunlight that reaches the Earth's surface, variations of which may cause animals to undergo hibernation or to migrate, and plants to be dormant. Various cultures define the number and nature of seasons based on regional variations, and as such there are a number of both modern and historical definitions of the seasons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/ChangingSeasons_NH_01.png/330px-ChangingSeasons_NH_01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Season","wikidata":"Q24384"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Darwin_thunderstorm.jpg/500px-Darwin_thunderstorm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Darwin_thunderstorm.jpg/500px-Darwin_thunderstorm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A wet-season storm at night in Darwin, Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADarwin_thunderstorm.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/During_the_rainy_season_Chattogram%2CBangladesh.jpg/500px-During_the_rainy_season_Chattogram%2CBangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/During_the_rainy_season_Chattogram%2CBangladesh.jpg/1280px-During_the_rainy_season_Chattogram%2CBangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/During_the_rainy_season_Chattogram%2CBangladesh.jpg/500px-During_the_rainy_season_Chattogram%2CBangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Monsoon floods in Bangladesh","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADuring_the_rainy_season_Chattogram%2CBangladesh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/MeanMonthlyP.gif/500px-MeanMonthlyP.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/MeanMonthlyP.gif/500px-MeanMonthlyP.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Long-term mean precipitation by month","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMeanMonthlyP.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/EatonCanyonWetSeason.jpg/500px-EatonCanyonWetSeason.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/EatonCanyonWetSeason.jpg/1280px-EatonCanyonWetSeason.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/EatonCanyonWetSeason.jpg/500px-EatonCanyonWetSeason.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A normally dry, chaparral ecosystem following a successful wet season in Southern California","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEatonCanyonWetSeason.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8d/East_-_Guinean_Savanna_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8d/East_-_Guinean_Savanna_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Equatorial savanna in the East Province of Cameroon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEast_-_Guinean_Savanna_001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Monsoon_clouds_arriving_at_Port_Blair%2C_Andaman.jpg/500px-Monsoon_clouds_arriving_at_Port_Blair%2C_Andaman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Monsoon_clouds_arriving_at_Port_Blair%2C_Andaman.jpg/500px-Monsoon_clouds_arriving_at_Port_Blair%2C_Andaman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Monsoon clouds arriving at Port Blair, Andaman, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonsoon_clouds_arriving_at_Port_Blair%2C_Andaman.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Monsoon_clouds_Lucknow.JPG/500px-Monsoon_clouds_Lucknow.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Monsoon_clouds_Lucknow.JPG/1280px-Monsoon_clouds_Lucknow.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Monsoon_clouds_Lucknow.JPG/500px-Monsoon_clouds_Lucknow.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Monsoon clouds over Lucknow, Uttar Pradesh, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonsoon_clouds_Lucknow.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Saison_des_pluies_%C3%A0_Mayotte.jpg/500px-Saison_des_pluies_%C3%A0_Mayotte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Saison_des_pluies_%C3%A0_Mayotte.jpg/1280px-Saison_des_pluies_%C3%A0_Mayotte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"http